  "notes": "Transcribed 2026-11-13 from the official Southern Utah University 2026-2027 General Catalog (current edition, catoid=28) Studio Arts - Ceramics Emphasis (BFA) program page and its linked official degree map, 'Studio Arts Degree Maps (2026-2027)', tab 'Ceramics (Campus)', last updated/reviewed August 3, 2026 (the workbook Index lists Online as N/A for this program). Semester placement is the university's official sample 4-year campus academic plan (SUU Program Maps, 2026-2027), which the source itself labels a guide only; students confirm specifics in Degree Works with a Student Success Advisor. The catalog prints 'Total Credits, BFA Degree: 120', which the map matches exactly (16/16/15/16/13/15/15/14). The map exercises the full catalog curriculum of 81 credits: BFA Art Foundation 25 (ART 1090 at 1 credit, ART 1110/1120/1130/1800/2110/2210, ARTH 2710/2720) and the Ceramics Emphasis 56 (ART 1610/3080/3610/3620/3720/4610/4620, ART 4630 taken two times for 6 credits per the catalog, ART 4790/4800, ARTH 3750, CHEM 1010 with CHEM 1015 lab at 1 credit, GEO 1090 with GEO 1095 lab at 1 credit, ART 4990 at 0 credits, and the catalog's two 'Complete Two of the Following (6 Credits)' blocks, exercised by the map's two generic 'Major Elective' rows (sculpture block) and its two Fall Year 4 art history rows). CATALOG-VS-MAP CODE CONFLICT, disclosed not reconciled: the map prints the Spring Year 3 Multi-Media Sculpture course as 'ART 3270' while the catalog prints the course as ART 3720; the catalog code ART 3720 is recorded here. Catalog titles are recorded where the map abbreviates (ART 1800). Per the catalog, all courses must be passed with a C (2.0) or better to be counted (the catalog page's Program Information prints this rule with the word 'minor'), transfer students must complete at least 50% of their art credits at SUU, and BFA students must apply for acceptance to the program during their sophomore year (the map carries a 'BFA Program Application Due' banner in Year 2). ART 4990 Senior BFA Exhibition is a 0-credit requirement, recorded as required_zero.",
